<div class="side-by-side">
  <div>
<div class="side-by-side">
  <div>
    <p class="big">The Challenge</p>
    <p>The Army National Guard wanted to use Code Red to launch its own branded tournament series. We had to fit military branding into an Apex Legends tournament in a way that felt natural to players.</p>

  </div>
  <div>
    <p class="big">The Solution</p>
    <p>We developed a sub-brand, Code Freedom. Our trailer for the event placed Code Freedom inside the world of Apex Legends using motion tracking and environment compositing.</p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <p class="big">The Impact</p>
    <p>Code Freedom became an established sub-brand within Code Red. It gave the Army National Guard a lasting entry point into esports marketing, and the Guard extended its partnership with us <a href="/projects/code-freedom-2024/">for another two years.</a> </p>
  </div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div>
  <h2>The Impact</h2>
  <p>
    Code Red grew into a proven marketing label. Verizon's Fortnite series alone drove 2.3M+ social views, the Hi-Chew tournament produced a new brand ambassador, and the Army National Guard's Code Freedom campaign was built as a sub-brand of Code Red.
  </p>

